      "hints": [
        "Find stationary point $B(2, 3)$ from $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2x - 4 = 0$.",
        "Midpoint of $A(4, 7)$ and $B(2, 3)$ is $(3, 5)$.",
        "Substitute $(3, 5)$ into line $y = mx - 2 \\implies m = \\frac{7}{3}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Find the stationary point $B$ of the curve $y = x^2 - 4x + 7$ by setting the derivative to zero:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2x - 4 = 0 \\implies x = 2$$\n$$y = 2^2 - 4(2) + 7 = 3 \\implies B = (2, 3)$$",
        "Calculate the midpoint $M$ of $A(4, 7)$ and $B(2, 3)$:\n$$M = \\left(\\frac{4 + 2}{2}, \\frac{7 + 3}{2}\\right) = (3, 5)$$",
        "Substitute $(3, 5)$ into the line equation $y = mx - 2$ to find $m$:\n$$5 = m(3) - 2 \\implies 3m = 7 \\implies m = \\frac{7}{3}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Line Parameter from Midpoint": "Finds stationary point $B(2, 3)$ (B2). Finds midpoint $(3, 5)$ (B1 FT). Solves for $m = \\frac{7}{3}$ (B1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
